# Response headers for the prerendered asset tree.
#
# Cloudflare Workers assets were serving everything under /_next/static/ as
# `public, max-age=0, must-revalidate`, which is Next.js's default for HTML but
# wrong for these: every file in this tree has a content hash in its filename
# (chunks, media, and the build-id directory that holds the manifests), so the
# bytes at a given URL can never change. max-age=0 made every one of the 16
# assets revalidate on every visit instead of being served from the browser's
# own cache, which costs a conditional round trip per file for no benefit.
#
# `immutable` is the correct signal and lets the browser skip revalidation
# entirely. The build-id directory changes name on each deploy, so a new build
# produces new URLs rather than new bytes behind old ones.
#
# Scoped to /_next/static/ on purpose. The HTML and the JSON/XML routes are
# served by the Worker rather than from this directory, and their caching is
# already correct — pages are `s-maxage=31536000` against a CDN that is
# expected to revalidate them. Widening this to /* would make the un-hashed
# files here (favicon.ico, the verification .html) immutable too, which is not
# true of them.
/_next/static/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
